@startuml
title OpenGL Graphics Pipeline

skinparam linetype ortho
top to bottom direction

rectangle "1. Vertex Specification\n\nMesh data loaded from OBJ:\nVertices, Normals, UVs,\nIndices" as VSPEC #LightYellow

rectangle "2. Vertex Shader\n\nRuns once per vertex.\nModel * View * Projection\ntransformations.\nOutputs Clip-Space Position." as VSHADER #LightBlue

rectangle "3. Tessellation Shader\n(Optional)\n\nSubdivide geometry\nfor additional detail." as TESS #LightGray

rectangle "4. Fragment Shader\n(Optional)\n\nCreate, modify,\nor discard primitives." as GSHADER #LightGray

rectangle "5. Clipping\n\nClip primitives against\nview frustum planes.\nMay generate new vertices." as CLIP #LightYellow

rectangle "6. Perspective Divide\n\n(x,y,z,w) ->\n(x/w,y/w,z/w)\nProduces NDC coordinates." as PDIV #LightYellow

rectangle "7. Viewport Transform\n\nNDC -> Screen Coordinates\nMaps [-1,1] to pixels." as VIEWPORT #LightYellow

rectangle "8. Primitive Assembly\n\nIndex buffer groups\nvertices into triangles,\nlines, or points." as PRIM #LightYellow

rectangle "9. Rasterization\n\nDetermine covered pixels.\nCompute barycentric\ncoordinates.\nGenerate fragments." as RAST #LightYellow

rectangle "10. Fragment Shader\n\nRuns per fragment.\nTexture sampling,\nlighting, shading." as FSHADER #LightBlue

rectangle "11. Per-Fragment Operations

Depth Test
Stencil Test
Blending
MSAA Resolve

Determines whether
the fragment survives
and how it combines
with existing pixels." as PFO #LightYellow

rectangle "12. Framebuffer

GPU memory containing:

• Color Buffer
• Depth Buffer
• Stencil Buffer

Stores the final image
being rendered." as FB #LightGreen

rectangle "13. Display / Screen

Monitor scans the
framebuffer contents
and emits photons.

This is the image
the user sees." as DISPLAY #LightBlue

PFO --> FB
FB --> DISPLAY
VSPEC --> VSHADER
VSHADER --> TESS
TESS --> GSHADER
GSHADER --> CLIP
CLIP --> PDIV
PDIV --> VIEWPORT
VIEWPORT --> PRIM
PRIM --> RAST
RAST --> FSHADER
FSHADER --> PFO
PFO --> FB

@enduml